# Advisories accepted with a written reason, reviewed whenever this file is
# touched. Everything here must also appear in the CASA evidence pack under
# 6.1.1 with the same justification.
#
# github.com/dgrijalva/jwt-go CVE-2020-26160 (HIGH):
# Accepted because this is a transitive dependency pulled in only by
# github.com/meszmate/apple-go, and the vulnerable code path is JWT validation.
# Our code uses apple-go solely for Apple client-secret signing, not for JWT
# validation, so the vulnerable parser/validator is never reached. The package
# is unmaintained and apple-go has not migrated; replacing it would require
# application-code changes to Apple Sign-in. Tracked for replacement in a
# dedicated auth improvement, not as a CI green-washing exercise.
#
# The four advisories with no upstream fix
# (github.com/xuri/excelize GO-2026-6452 and the three hamba/avro decoder
# advisories) are Go-module findings that govulncheck reports and Trivy's
# severity filter does not raise, so suppressing them here would be
# suppressing nothing. They are justified in the evidence pack instead.
